# Secrets for the cloud environment's API credentials section (cloud
# environment menu -> Edit -> API credentials). If your environment doesn't
# offer that section, use the Environment variables field instead, and keep in
# mind that anyone who can edit the environment can read those values.
#
# Add only the credentials for services you use, and give each token the
# narrowest scope that still works. Never commit real values to this repo.
#
# Not needed here:
#   GitHub: `gh` and git already authenticate through the Claude GitHub App via
#     the session's proxy. Don't set GH_TOKEN / GITHUB_TOKEN, because that would
#     replace the app's credentials (see .env.example).
#   Sprites: use the Sprites connector on claude.ai rather than the sprite CLI.
#     setup.sh no longer installs the CLI, so no SPRITES_TOKEN is needed.

# Fly.io CLI (`fly` / flyctl). Create one with `fly tokens create deploy` (one
# app) or `fly tokens create org` (all apps in an org).
FLY_API_TOKEN=FlyV1 fm2_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
